A||||10||Bazooka||Wiring Diagrams for Conversions||||1||
Z||000000||Bazooka||06-25-2001||08:09 PM||||List,<BR>   Anyone know where there would be any Wiring Diagrams for the 3800SC, Northstar, and or SBC? Does anyone make Custom Harnesses for these conversions? I'd be interested in both the 'Piggyback designs for the ECM and Total Replacement PCM such as the Caddy's. TIA.<BR> <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-25-2001||08:16 PM||||ACE makes wiring harnesses for the 3800 Fiero conversion. $1500 I've been told.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bazooka||06-25-2001||11:33 PM||||Lars,<BR>   Do you know if that is using only a 'Donor Cars' computer? Has Ace worked out all the running and starting problems on the 3800? $1500 is a lot of 'Jolly Bucks'. Even Northstar Harnesses can be had for less than $1000. Is the 3800 more complicated than the Northstar? Maybe the Supercharged one. Thanks for the info. <BR>*************************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>ACE makes wiring harnesses for the 3800 Fiero conversion. $1500 I've been told.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||06-26-2001||09:01 AM||||I understand that the donor car's computer is used. Supposedly they (ACE) have all the "bugs" worked out so that it works.  I haven't heard of anyone just plugging it all together and having everything work the first time.<P>You'd need to call the experts as to the difficulty factor.  Chris Moore with the Northstars conversion.  I know Bob Steiger was finishing up a 3800 s/c in a black GT and was always finding little things (time consuming) electrical glitches that had to be worked out so that it all went together correctly.  Lots of wires to match up.  God forbid if the Fiero had had some creative wiring in its history then try to convert to a 3800 engine.<P>The 3800s are real fast, but I don't know where you can easily use all the power, unless you have $$ for tires as you smoke them at launch.  Not my style any more.||||reg||1
Z||000004||gabriel||06-26-2001||10:40 AM||||&gt;Does anyone make Custom Harnesses for these conversions? <P>Cris West at cwestco does the 3800 harness, for way less, I believe, than that amount.  You use the donor PCM and the Fiero body ECM.<P>Use the search function with " 3800SC "<P> For the SBC, V-8 Archie would be the man.<P>As far as wiring diagrams, just call your local GM dealer's parts desk.  You would need to know the exact model & year.||||reg||1
Z||000005||cowans||06-26-2001||11:03 AM||||For the SBC, Archie posted an explanation with pics about 6 months ago....do a search on V8 wiring.<BR>Sandy||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bazooka||06-26-2001||03:21 PM||||As for the SBC, I presently have a "Street and Performance" Harness in mine, but I was hoping to find a 'Lead Data' type of diagram and also a schematic that would show the Tie In Points and which wires are used from the Fiero and which are from the New ECM/new engine. I wonder if any one has used "Fully Insulated" connections and terminals? <BR>***********************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cowans:<BR><B>For the SBC, Archie posted an explanation with pics about 6 months ago....do a search on V8 wiring.<BR>Sandy</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||rockcrawl||06-26-2001||09:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>and also a schematic that would show the Tie In Points and which wires are used from the Fiero and which are from the New ECM/new engine.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I have some info posted on my website that might help you out: <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/fierowiring.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/fierowiring.htm</A> <BR>I also have the TPI diagrams if you need them, I will need to scan them. What year TPI system are you running?||||reg||1
Z||000008||00lE||06-27-2001||08:00 AM||||I can help with the SBC, but the others are a bit rare.  The exact diagrams would of course depend on the ECM you would be using.  There are quite a few located here :<P> <A HREF="ftp://ftp.diy-efi.org/pub/gmecm/manuals/" TARGET=_blank>ftp://ftp.diy-efi.org/pub/gmecm/manuals/</A> <P>The 1227730 ECM is one of the most popular for the TPI V8's :<P><A HREF="ftp://ftp.diy-efi.org/pub/gmecm/manuals/1227730/" TARGET=_blank>ftp://ftp.diy-efi.org/pub/gmecm/manuals/1227730/</A><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 00lE (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jay||06-27-2001||03:37 PM||||Howel Engine Developements makes the harness for the Northstar/Fiero conversion for under $1000 US||||reg||1
Z||000010||Bazooka||06-27-2001||06:35 PM||||Rock,<BR>   Thanks for the great references and articles. I'm sure to refer to them. I have a 90 TPI with a Speed/Density system. I wanted to see what harness changes I would need to go from the SBC to the Northstar (4.6) in my Fiero? Thanks for your help<BR>********************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR>[B] [QUOTE]and also a schematic that would show the Tie In Points and which wires are used from the Fiero and which are from the New ECM/new engine.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I have some info posted on my website that might help you out: <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/fierowiring.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/fierowiring.htm</A> <BR>I also have the TPI diagrams if you need them, I will need to scan them. What year TPI system are you running?<P>||||reg||1
